 "rationale": "Ladder c18 shelf-packed each idx stack's h0 halves and h1 on different shelves (h0->h1 centre up to 2.4 mm, stscan missing>405). Here each stack is one frame (h1 + ra + rb, 4.32/6.05 um apart, h0->h1 centre <= 331 um). Banks keep their ladder sites (q_b011 pair7 and the q_b010__physical_v1 bank rows 1 and 3 move to open frame slots), so plan-station counts stay as bound; frames are placed where their soft relay counts reach their windows (1-reg links <= 810 um, 3-reg <= 1620 um), frame rows sit between the 250-um die cut lines (or put a line through the 4.32-um h1/h0 gap) so no partition cut-segment ratio rises above max(0.6, t19), the clock tap stays in a street, and ft-slot / plan-station register sites covered by a frame are re-sited on free sites with the same count (hops <= 405 um, first/last hop measured to the far end of the window)."
